 "note_en": "The pattern 把 + object + verb + complement puts the object before the verb when what matters is what was done to it and the state it's now in. 把材料整理得整整齐齐 \"put the documents in perfect order\": not just \"sorted them,\" but sorted them so they're now neat. The verb after 把 never stands bare: it's followed by a result (整理得整整齐齐), a direction (放进了箱子), or 了.",
